VERSION 3.4 – Query Execution Pipeline

Context

After completing the Retrieval Engine implementation, the runtime
execution pipeline of the Knowledge Engine was finalized.

Goal

Provide a deterministic orchestration layer that coordinates all
engine components during query execution.

Implemented Components

QueryPipeline

Central orchestrator executing the engine pipeline:

Query
→ Intent Engine
→ Role Engine
→ Retrieval Engine
→ Scoring Engine
→ Perspective Orchestrator
→ Context Builder
→ Prompt Governance
→ LLM

QueryContext

A central state object was introduced to capture the full execution
state of a query.

The QueryContext stores:

query
intent
role
retrieval_result
ranked_documents
perspective
context_package
prompt
response

Benefits

- simplified pipeline structure
- improved debugging
- easier explainability
- support for audit logging

Retrieval Decision Log

A new audit component logs retrieval decisions for each query.

Logged data includes:

query
intent
role
document scores
context chunks
sources

Purpose

- explainability
- debugging
- governance transparency